🚀 Week 5 – Day 2 Importing Packages & Naming Conventions in Java ☕

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Java programs often use classes from different packages.

👉 To access those classes, Java provides the `import` statement.

Following proper naming conventions also makes code:

✔ Readable
✔ Maintainable
✔ Professional

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📦 1. Importing Packages

The `import` keyword is used to access classes and interfaces from another package.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="i1"
import packageName.ClassName;
```

---

📌 Example

```java id="i2"
import java.util.Scanner;

class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Enter Name:");
        String name = sc.nextLine();

        System.out.println(name);
    }
}
```

---

🔹 Import Entire Package

```java id="i3"
import java.util.*;
```

👉 Imports all classes from the package.

---

🔹 Multiple Imports

```java id="i4"
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;
```

---

🔹 Fully Qualified Name

Instead of importing:

```java id="i5"
java.util.Scanner sc =
        new java.util.Scanner(System.in);
```

---

🎯 Advantages of Import

✔ Cleaner code
✔ Easier class access
✔ Better readability

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Common Built-in Packages

| Package     | Purpose                 |
| ----------- | ----------------------- |
| `java.lang` | Core Java classes       |
| `java.util` | Collections & utilities |
| `java.io`   | Input and Output        |
| `java.sql`  | Database connectivity   |
| `java.net`  | Networking              |

---

🔍 Special Note

Classes from `java.lang` are imported automatically.

Example:

```java id="i6"
String name = "Java";
System.out.println(name);
```

No import needed.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🏷️ 2. Java Naming Conventions

Naming conventions are recommended standards for naming Java elements.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Class Names

Use **PascalCase**.

```java id="n1"
class StudentManagementSystem {
}
```

✔ First letter of every word is capitalized.

---

🔹 Interface Names

Also use **PascalCase**.

```java id="n2"
interface Printable {
}
```

---

🔹 Method Names

Use **camelCase**.

```java id="n3"
void calculateSalary() {
}
```

---

🔹 Variable Names

Use **camelCase**.

```java id="n4"
int studentAge;
String employeeName;
```

---

🔹 Constant Names

Use **UPPER_CASE**.

```java id="n5"
final int MAX_SIZE = 100;
```

---

🔹 Package Names

Use **lowercase letters**.

```java id="n6"
package com.company.project;
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 Naming Convention Summary

| Element   | Convention | Example             |
| --------- | ---------- | ------------------- |
| Class     | PascalCase | StudentRecord       |
| Interface | PascalCase | Runnable            |
| Method    | camelCase  | displayData()       |
| Variable  | camelCase  | totalMarks          |
| Constant  | UPPER_CASE | MAX_VALUE           |
| Package   | lowercase  | com.example.project |

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Using spaces in names
❌ Starting variable names with numbers
❌ Using inconsistent naming styles
❌ Using uppercase package names

---

🧠 Real Insight

👉 Good naming conventions make large projects easier to understand and maintain.

Most companies enforce coding standards during development.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ `import` allows access to external package classes
✔ `java.lang` is imported automatically
✔ Use PascalCase for classes and interfaces
✔ Use camelCase for methods and variables
✔ Use UPPER_CASE for constants

